  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the thinking man scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man pointing to his head, as his pose is used to frame the text as an authoritative or revelatory insight. The user is implicitly positioned as the one who is 'thinking' or 'having an epiphany' about the causal link between Islam's age and terrorism, as presented in the text. The man's contemplative expression and gesture create a direct visual link to the user's own cognitive process, suggesting the user is the one who has discovered or is being led to discover this 'truth'.",
